+# Tool Input Validation
+
+| Field  | Value                |
+| ------ | -------------------- |
+| Issue  | re-cinq/HALEngine#37 |
+| Status | Draft                |
+
+Tool definitions use JSON Schema as the single contract sent to providers and enforced by the registry before an executor receives a model tool call.
+
+## Registry validation
+
+`ToolRegistry.execute` validates a resolved tool definition's `inputSchema` before it invokes the executor. A missing required field, wrong declared type, or value outside an enum returns a `ToolResponse` whose result identifies the property and failed constraint without including an input value; unknown properties pass through unchanged. ([validated by: rejects schema-invalid input before the executor while preserving valid unknown fields](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L24))
+
+## Schema lifecycle
+
+Registration compiles a static definition's schema so an invalid schema fails at startup with the tool name and the schema compiled at registration is reused across executions. ([validated by: rejects an invalid static schema when the named tool is registered](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L67)) ([validated by: keeps a static schema compiled at registration across executions](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L78)) A function-valued definition validates each call against the schema it resolves for that call. ([validated by: uses the schema resolved for each dynamic tool invocation](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L96))
